    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "(** * Enumerations by the natural numbers *)",
      "messages": [],
      "goals": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "text",
      "contents": "\n\n(** We enumerate pairs of natural numbers, and deduce that a product of two images of the natural numbers is again an image of the natural numbers.  Such surjections from the natural numbers are what bounded search needs, see [minimal_n_alt_type]. *)\n\n"
    },
    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "From HoTT Require Import Basics Types.Prod Truncations.Core Spaces.Nat.Core.",
      "messages": [],
      "goals": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "text",
      "contents": "\n"
    },
    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "From HoTT Require Import Modalities.ReflectiveSubuniverse.",
      "messages": [],
      "goals": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "text",
      "contents": "\n\n"
    },
    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "Local Open Scope nat_scope.",
      "messages": [],
      "goals": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "text",
      "contents": "\n\n(** ** Enumerating pairs *)\n\n(** We enumerate pairs of natural numbers diagonal by diagonal.  Here the [m]th diagonal consists of the pairs [(a, b)] with [a + b = m]. *)\n"
    },
    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "Fixpoint nat_unpair (n : nat) : nat * nat\n  := match n with\n     | 0 => (0, 0)\n     | S n => match nat_unpair n with\n             | (0, b) => (S b, 0)\n             | (S a, b) => (a, S b)\n             end\n     end.",
      "messages": [],
      "goals": []
    },
    {
      "_type": "text",
      "contents": "\n\n(** If we hit the end of a diagonal, we hit everything else on the diagonal. *)\n"
    },
    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "Local Definition nat_unpair_hit_diagonal (a b : nat) (p : {n : nat & nat_unpair n = (a + b, 0)})\n  : {m : nat & nat_unpair m = (a, b)}.",
      "messages": [],
      "goals": [
        {
          "_type": "goal",
          "name": null,
          "conclusion": "{m : nat & nat_unpair m = (a, b)}",
          "hypotheses": [
            {
              "_type": "hypothesis",
              "names": [
                "a",
                "b"
              ],
              "body": null,
              "type": "nat"
            },
            {
              "_type": "hypothesis",
              "names": [
                "p"
              ],
              "body": null,
              "type": "{n : nat & nat_unpair n = (a + b, 0)}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "text",
      "contents": "\n"
    },
    {
      "_type": "sentence",
      "contents": "Proof.",
      "messages": [],
